# OQ-4, L §5.18 The world of an ask: "In a joint model a value pin or an as if may name a member's row (§6.1); like
# every pin, it sets that ask's world only and changes no member's file". The joint model of L6_1_joint: with
# a.rate = 0.2 ana's tax[2026] is 120 000 * 0.2 = 24 000 PLN (k3), as if {a.rate = 0.25} 30 000 PLN (k4); a.q still
# gives 14 400 PLN. k1/k2 bind over the member's index a.yrs (L §2.3 bind takes a member's index).
=== options pin=bytes
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "ana.tally" sha256 "26a08dc22b514dc0b6eb7c1263103f06b216244b4ed980752bbc810412d05e45"
  use b = "ben.tally" sha256 "a8bf3b260e60f625766da425a660f922557f525c28dcf8ed70567ec64d600ccc"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index jy = year 2025..2027

def income_sum[y in jy]: num PLN = a.income[y] + b.income at reader

ask j1: income_sum[y] for y in jy law 2026-12-31
ask j2: a.tax[2026] law 2026-12-31
ask j3: a.rate law 2026-12-31
ask k1: a.income[y] for y in a.yrs law 2026-12-31
ask k2: sum(a.income[y] for y in a.yrs) law 2026-12-31
ask k3: a.tax[2026] with a.rate = 0.2 law 2026-12-31
ask k4: a.tax[2026] as if {a.rate = 0.25} law 2026-12-31
=== ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index yrs = year 2025..2027
input income[y in yrs]: money PLN
input rate: num
def tax[y in yrs]: num PLN = income[y] * rate at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2025..
  known 2025-01-01
  income[2025] = 100 000.00 PLN
  income[2026] = 120 000.00 PLN
  income[2027] = 130 000.00 PLN
  rate = 0.12

ask q: tax[2026] law 2026-12-31
=== ben.tally
model ben
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input income: money PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs 2025..
  known 2025-01-01
  income = 80 000.00 PLN

ask q: income law 2026-12-31
=== expect k1 k2 k3 k4 a.q
k1 (y = 2025): 100 000.00 PLN
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-10-20
k1 (y = 2026): 120 000.00 PLN
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-10-20
k1 (y = 2027): 130 000.00 PLN
  held: a.income[2027] = 130 000.00 PLN (a.v), read for 2027
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-10-20
k2: 350 000.00 PLN
  held: a.income[2027] = 130 000.00 PLN (a.v), read for 2027
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-10-20
k3: 24 000 PLN
  pinned: a.rate = 0.2
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-10-20
k4: 30 000 PLN
  pinned: a.rate = 0.25
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-10-20
a.q: 14 400 PLN
  held: rate = 0.12 (v), read for 2026-12-31
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-10-20
